==Enemy==
Compared to Bore, Dread Bore gains the usual Zombie abilities of burrow + revive and moves significantly faster, but its other stats are more or less the same. However, because there are far fewer [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie cats]] than there are [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]], it will often prove to be much harder to deal with. Its money drop is notably quite high for a Zombie enemy.

==Strategy==
It is critical to use anti-Zombie [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] that can inflict status effects on Dread Bore, bringing it to a halt. But beware, for this enemy will burrow under your front line, blocking the way and attacking incoming units. This can be a problem when combined with other enemies that you need a consistent stream of meatshields for, like [[Lord Gravey]].

To keep Dread Bore at bay, options from the [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] category include [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]],  [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]] and Talented [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]]. Alternatively, you can also use [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] to resurface, knockback and temporary freeze it too. In terms of [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]], anti-Zombies like [[Queen Reika (Uber Rare Cat)|Pharaoh Reika]], [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Atlantis Logistix]] and [[EVA Unit-01 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-01]] are good options for delivering massive damage to it.

